WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.979
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:08.862
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.162 --> 00:00:14.009
Unit five: Food & Meals. Today you will talk about food using some and any.

4
00:00:14.309 --> 00:00:17.019
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:17.967 --> 00:00:21.513
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:23.316
Cuisine.

7
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:27.001
Cuisine means a style of cooking from a country.

8
00:00:27.617 --> 00:00:29.930
Khmer cuisine uses lots of herbs.

9
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:32.856
Your turn. Say: Cuisine.

10
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:36.666
Cuisine.

11
00:00:37.417 --> 00:00:38.244
Flavor.

12
00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:41.006
Flavor means the taste of food.

13
00:00:41.617 --> 00:00:43.779
Lemongrass gives a fresh flavor.

14
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:47.105
Your turn. Say: Flavor.

15
00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:50.910
Flavor.

16
00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:52.744
Spicy.

17
00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.620
Spicy means hot because of chili or pepper.

18
00:00:57.217 --> 00:00:59.367
This curry is too spicy for me.

19
00:00:59.983 --> 00:01:02.647
Your turn. Say: Spicy.

20
00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.664
Spicy.

21
00:01:07.417 --> 00:01:08.267
Sour.

22
00:01:09.283 --> 00:01:11.759
Sour means with a sharp taste like a lime.

23
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.605
Samlor machu is a sour soup.

24
00:01:15.217 --> 00:01:17.648
Your turn. Say: Sour.

25
00:01:20.500 --> 00:01:21.501
Sour.

26
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:23.286
Nutritious.

27
00:01:24.283 --> 00:01:27.525
Nutritious means full of things that keep you healthy.

28
00:01:28.117 --> 00:01:29.814
Vegetables are nutritious.

29
00:01:30.417 --> 00:01:33.232
Your turn. Say: Nutritious.

30
00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:37.277
Nutritious.

31
00:01:38.017 --> 00:01:39.018
Snack.

32
00:01:40.017 --> 00:01:43.119
Snack means a small amount of food between meals.

33
00:01:43.717 --> 00:01:45.554
I eat a banana as a snack.

34
00:01:46.150 --> 00:01:48.651
Your turn. Say: Snack.

35
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:52.280
Snack.

36
00:01:53.017 --> 00:01:53.890
Portion.

37
00:01:54.883 --> 00:01:57.370
Portion means the amount of food for one person.

38
00:01:57.983 --> 00:01:59.577
The portions here are big.

39
00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:02.499
Your turn. Say: Portion.

40
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:06.172
Portion.

41
00:02:06.917 --> 00:02:07.999
Appetite.

42
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:11.587
Appetite means the feeling that you want to eat.

43
00:02:12.183 --> 00:02:14.148
Sport gives me a big appetite.

44
00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.588
Your turn. Say: Appetite.

45
00:02:20.433 --> 00:02:21.516
Appetite.

46
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.030
Diet.

47
00:02:24.017 --> 00:02:26.272
Diet means the food you usually eat.

48
00:02:26.883 --> 00:02:29.440
A healthy diet has fruit and vegetables.

49
00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:32.551
Your turn. Say: Diet.

50
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.134
Diet.

51
00:02:36.883 --> 00:02:37.757
Craving.

52
00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:41.493
Craving means a strong wish for a certain food.

53
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:44.629
I have a craving for mango sticky rice.

54
00:02:45.217 --> 00:02:47.765
Your turn. Say: Craving.

55
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:51.439
Craving.

56
00:02:52.183 --> 00:02:53.022
Homemade.

57
00:02:54.017 --> 00:02:56.492
Homemade means made at home, not in a shop.

58
00:02:57.083 --> 00:02:59.048
Homemade food is the best.

59
00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:02.140
Your turn. Say: Homemade.

60
00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:05.862
Homemade.

61
00:03:06.617 --> 00:03:07.734
Leftovers.

62
00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:11.852
Leftovers means food that is not eaten after a meal.

63
00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:14.496
We had leftovers for breakfast.

64
00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:17.782
Your turn. Say: Leftovers.

65
00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:21.843
Leftovers.

66
00:03:22.633 --> 00:03:26.203
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:03:27.050 --> 00:03:29.386
Visal, do you have any snacks in your bag?

68
00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:33.748
Yes, I have some fruit and some nuts.

69
00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.861
Is there any rice left from lunch?

70
00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:42.112
No, there aren't any leftovers. I had a big appetite!

71
00:03:43.217 --> 00:03:44.810
What's your favorite cuisine?

72
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:50.252
Khmer cuisine! I love sour and spicy flavors.

73
00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.005
Part three: grammar.

74
00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:57.730
Grammar focus: Countable and uncountable plus some and any.

75
00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.136
Look at the pattern.

76
00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:01.304
I have some snacks.

77
00:04:02.217 --> 00:04:03.903
I don't have any leftovers.

78
00:04:04.817 --> 00:04:06.282
Is there any rice?

79
00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:12.579
Countable nouns can be plural (snacks). Uncountable nouns have no plural (rice, water).

80
00:04:13.317 --> 00:04:16.619
Be careful! Don't say: I don't have some snacks.

81
00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:21.031
Say: I don't have any snacks.

82
00:04:21.331 --> 00:04:24.038
Use 'any' in negative sentences and questions.

83
00:04:24.833 --> 00:04:27.346
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.529
Our Family Meals.

85
00:04:29.829 --> 00:04:32.897
I love spicy and sour flavors in Khmer cuisine.

86
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:36.898
My mother always makes nutritious homemade meals.

87
00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.898
We usually have some rice, some fish and some vegetables.

88
00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:45.339
We don't buy any junk food, but we eat some fruit as a snack.

89
00:04:46.333 --> 00:04:49.076
If there are any leftovers, we eat them the next day.

90
00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:54.192
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:04:55.050 --> 00:04:56.562
I don't have blank money.

92
00:04:56.862 --> 00:04:59.726
A, any. B, some. C, a.

93
00:05:03.267 --> 00:05:05.011
The answer is A: any.

94
00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.939
A small amount of food between meals is a blank.

95
00:05:09.239 --> 00:05:12.637
A, snack. B, portion. C, cuisine.

96
00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.130
The answer is A: snack.

97
00:05:19.283 --> 00:05:21.596
Full of things that keep you healthy is blank.

98
00:05:21.896 --> 00:05:25.945
A, nutritious. B, spicy. C, sour.

99
00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.616
The answer is A: nutritious.

100
00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:35.777
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:05:36.617 --> 00:05:39.232
Describe your favorite meal and why you like it.

102
00:05:48.017 --> 00:05:49.343
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:05:49.643 --> 00:05:57.566
My favorite meal is fish amok with some rice. I like it because it has a rich flavor, and it's homemade by my mother.

104
00:05:57.866 --> 00:05:59.529
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:06:00.417 --> 00:06:05.739
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and countable and uncountable plus some and any.

106
00:06:06.039 --> 00:06:10.596
Today's value is healthy eating. Eat fruit and vegetables to grow strong.

107
00:06:10.896 --> 00:06:13.432
See you in Unit six. Goodbye!

108
00:06:13.732 --> 00:06:16.477
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

